# --- wk sysimage: every image built for the rpi5 -------------------------------
# Appended to the target's local.conf by `wk sysimage build`, last, so bitbake
# takes it. What belongs here is what the *board* requires of any image built
# for it; what a measurement wants belongs to the profile.

# The Pi 5 exists in two steppings and the firmware adapts one device tree to
# both: it loads broadcom/bcm2712-rpi-5-b.dtb, whose pinctrl nodes carry the C0
# layout, and on D0 silicon applies overlays/bcm2712d0.dtbo over it -- narrower
# GPIO banks (32/4 and 15/6), the two pinctrl nodes moved to
# `brcm,bcm2712d0-pinctrl` with a smaller register window, and vc4 to
# `brcm,bcm2712d0-vc6`.
#
# Without that overlay the kernel drives D0 hardware with C0 pin data
# (`brcm,bcm2712-pinctrl` maps to bcm2712_c0_plat_data,
# drivers/pinctrl/bcm/pinctrl-bcm2712.c), and the first pull-config write lands
# outside the window: an uncontainable SError, and a panic in
# bcm2712_pull_config_set before rootfs.
#
# The pinned kernel builds the overlay already -- its overlays Makefile lists
# bcm2712d0.dtbo -- and meta-raspberrypi's RPI_KERNEL_DEVICETREE_OVERLAYS is a
# hand-curated 52 of the 367 it compiles, which is the whole of what was
# missing. Shipping the D0 *base* tree instead does nothing: the firmware
# never asks for it by name (measured -- a card carrying
# bcm2712d0-rpi-5-b.dtb panics identically, rpi5, 2026-09-04).
RPI_KERNEL_DEVICETREE_OVERLAYS:append = " overlays/bcm2712d0.dtbo"
